{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Written on the Body", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Alexander Technique", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Giving Reasons", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use reason clauses to express the reasons for an action, or why a situation is the way it is.<br/>You use words like <span class=\"italic\">because</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in case</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">seeing that</span>  to introduce a reason clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Reason clauses are subordinate to the main clause. They state the reason why things are done, or what makes a situation the way it is.<br/> You can use the following words to introduce a reason clause:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She assumed that she would probably have to learn to live with the problem, seeing as she worked long hours and that her job was stressful.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "One day, seeing that Sherri was holding her neck stiffly, one of the other programmers asked her what was wrong.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">UseConnector\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"because\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to explain why something is the way it is\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Because</span> she is a computer programmer, Sherri is required to sit at a desk all day long.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since/as\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to introduce a reason that is already known\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Since</span>  her posture is far from perfect, she was not surprised when she began to notice pain in her neck and shoulders.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(just) in case\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about things that may possibly happen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I came over <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">in case</span> you needed some extra help.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"seeing that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to state that a situation is known\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Seeing that </span> you're here early, we'll be done before noon.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<br/>Read the following examples from the text:", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Personal Passive vs Impersonal Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the passive voice when the subject of a sentence is receiving an action rather than doing an action.<br/>You use the Impersonal Passive to report events in a more general, formal way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A passive sentence puts the emphasis on the object of the active sentence. When you use a passive sentence to report an event, the object of the active sentence now becomes the subject and focus of the passive sentence.<br/>You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the verb <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>Active sentence: <span class=\"italic\">The doctor gave Sherri a pain medication prescription .<br/>Passive sentence: <span class=\"italic\">Sherri was given a pain medication prescription by her doctor.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the Passive form to report events in an impersonal way. The subject is not specific, but general.<br/>You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">It is said</span>, <span class=\"italic\">It is reported</span> to introduce the Impersonal Passive form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is said</span> that the Alexander technique was developed by an actor, F.M Alexander. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Alexander technique is said to have been invented by F. M. Alexander (1869-1955). ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Alexander, who was reported to have been an extraordinary Shakespearean actor, tried to find a way to strengthen his voice without conventional medical care.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Alexander is said to have created a teaching method that encourages the body to work more efficiently and holistically.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Alexander technique is not easy, but it is said to be worth the effort.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "prescription", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a doctor's written order for medication", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She got a prescription for pain medication from her doctor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about health in the workplace.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pain medication", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a drug used to reduce pain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She took the pain medication because of her sore back.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "masseuse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who gives a massage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She saw a masseuse every week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ache", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pain that is continuous but not necessarily strong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She visited a good masseuse when the ache in her neck got very bad.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stiffly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in a rigid manner", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One day, seeing that Sherri was holding her neck stiffly, one of the other programmers asked her what was wrong.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chronic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "recurring", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sherri told him about her chronic neck and shoulder pain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "laryngitis", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an infection of the larynx", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After almost losing his voice from laryngitis, Alexander tried to find a way to strengthen his voice without conventional medical care.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lengthen", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make longer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When he learned to reduce neck tension and lengthen his spine, his vocal problem disappeared.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the bones that run down the center of the back; backbone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He found that his spine had become twisted over the years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "holistically", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to the entire system instead of the individual parts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Alexander is said to have created a teaching method that encourages the body to work more efficiently and holistically.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob03aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and research \u201cThe Alexander Technique.\u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a step-by-step guide explaining how to do at least three different exercises. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Using your guide, explain the three exercises to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research the Alexander Technique.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a step-by-step guide.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain the guide to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about health and wellness.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about the reason of an action or an event.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express what is said to have happened or report statements.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever had a work-related injury? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What's the best way to avoid back pain for those who work at a desk all day? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's find out how a person can fix a back 